DEFAULT_POLICIES = json.loads('[{"slug": "privacy-policy", "title": "Privacy & Data Protection Policy", "eyebrow": "Corporate Governance & Sustainability", "meta": "Approved by Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder & CEO · 25 October 2026", "summary": "Privacy & Data Protection Policy — official SpacePoint public information and contact details.", "content_html": "<p>Data Protection, Privacy &amp; Information Security Policy</p><p>Public policy · Approved for website publication</p><h2>1. Purpose and Scope</h2><p>SpacePoint is committed to protecting personal information and maintaining appropriate information security throughout its educational programs, events, products, websites, learning platforms, research collaborations, and business operations. This policy applies to SpacePoint personnel and, where relevant, its service providers and contractors. It is intended to serve as a public privacy notice and an organizational statement of minimum security commitments.</p><h2>2. Information We Collect</h2><p>Depending on the service, SpacePoint may collect names, contact details, organization or school affiliation, age or age range, parent/guardian and emergency contact details where necessary, enrollment and attendance records, project submissions, assessments and learning progress, photographs or recordings where authorized, payment and invoice records, professional correspondence, and technical records such as IP addresses, account identifiers, platform logs and device information. We seek to collect only information reasonably necessary for stated purposes.</p><h2>3. How We Use Information</h2><p>We use information to register participants; deliver workshops, competitions and courses; manage the SpacePoint learning platform; communicate schedules and progress; issue certifications; provide support; safeguard participants; manage transactions and contractual relationships; improve program quality using appropriate analysis; comply with legal obligations; and, where permitted, publish event stories or send marketing communications. We will not use information for materially incompatible purposes without an appropriate legal basis and notice.</p><h2>4. Lawful Processing and Choice</h2><p>We process personal data using an appropriate basis permitted by applicable law, which may include consent, the performance of a contract, compliance with legal duties, or other legally available grounds. Where consent is required, it should be specific and recorded, and individuals may withdraw it where applicable. Optional marketing communications and promotional image use are subject to appropriate choices.</p><h2>5. Children and Student Safeguarding</h2><p>For participants under 18, SpacePoint takes particular care to obtain appropriate authorization from a parent, guardian, school or other authorized institution as required by the activity and applicable law. Before using identifiable student photographs, testimonials, videos or work for promotional purposes, SpacePoint seeks appropriate permission. Student access is limited according to educational and operational needs. We do not intentionally collect more information about children than is necessary.</p><h2>6. Sharing and International Transfers</h2><p>Information may be shared on a need-to-know basis with authorized instructors, host institutions, event organizers, payment and technology providers, certificate issuers, professional advisers, and competent authorities when legally required. We require service providers handling personal information to apply appropriate confidentiality and security protections. Where data is transferred outside the UAE, SpacePoint will assess the applicable transfer requirements and use appropriate safeguards.</p><h2>7. Retention and Deletion</h2><p>We retain information only as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described, agreed contractual needs, dispute resolution, and applicable legal or accounting obligations. Retention periods vary by record type and will be set in an internal retention schedule. On expiry, information will be securely deleted, anonymized or archived where legally justified.</p><h2>8. Individual Privacy Rights</h2><p>Subject to applicable law and exceptions, individuals may request information about their data, access, correction, deletion, restriction or cessation of certain processing, transfer where applicable, and withdrawal of consent. Requests may be sent through the designated privacy contact listed below. SpacePoint will verify identity where necessary and respond within applicable legal requirements.</p><h2>9. Information Security Controls</h2><p>SpacePoint adopts risk-appropriate administrative, technical and physical safeguards, including least-privilege account access, strong authentication, role-based permissions, secure configuration and patching, appropriate encryption in transit and at rest, controlled sharing, backups, vendor assessment, staff confidentiality commitments, and secure disposal. Personnel are expected to report suspected security incidents promptly. Controls are reviewed as systems and risks evolve; no system can be guaranteed completely secure.</p><h2>10. Security Incidents</h2><p>Suspected personal-data breaches or unauthorized access must be escalated immediately to the designated information-security lead. SpacePoint will contain and investigate incidents, preserve relevant evidence, assess potential harm, and make notifications to affected individuals or competent authorities where legally required.</p><h2>11. Cookies and Third-Party Services</h2><p>SpacePoint websites and learning portals may use essential cookies and, where enabled, analytics or other optional technologies. Any non-essential technologies will be described through an appropriate cookie notice or consent mechanism where required. Linked third-party services have their own policies.</p><h2>12. Contact and Updates</h2><p>Privacy and security requests: info@spacepoint.ae. Company: SpacePoint (UAE-based organization; registered entity name and address to be confirmed on the website before publication), United Arab Emirates. Website: https://spacepoint.ae. SpacePoint may update this policy as operational, legal or technical requirements evolve, identifying the effective date of the current approved version.</p><h2>Policy accountability and approval</h2><p>Policy owner: SpacePoint management (designated policy owner to be assigned internally). Approved by: Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder &amp; CEO. Review cycle: At least annually or sooner if legal or operational requirements change.</p><h2>Publication, Contacts and Approval</h2><p>Approved by: Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder &amp; CEO, SpacePoint.</p><p>Publication date: 25 October 2026. Review: At least annually and when relevant legal or operational changes occur.</p><p>Primary contact: info@spacepoint.ae. Secondary contact / escalation: a.alsalmani@spacepoint.ae.</p><p>For access, correction, withdrawal of consent or other privacy-related requests, email info@spacepoint.ae with sufficient detail to help locate the relevant records. Please avoid sending passwords or unnecessary sensitive information by email.</p>", "display_order": 1, "is_active": true, "show_in_footer": true}, {"slug": "terms-of-service", "title": "Terms & Conditions of Service", "eyebrow": "Legal Compliance", "meta": "Last updated: April 1, 2026 · SpacePoint FZC", "summary": "Terms and conditions governing the use of SpacePoint website, workshops, SatKit educational hardware, and learning programs.", "content_html": "<div class=\\"flex items-center gap-4 p-4 rounded-2xl bg-space-purple/10 border border-space-purple/20\\">\\n          <div class=\\"w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-space-accent/20 flex items-center justify-center text-space-accent flex-shrink-0\\">\\n            <svg class=\\"w-6 h-6\\" fill=\\"none\\" stroke=\\"currentColor\\" viewBox=\\"0 0 24 24\\">\\n              <path stroke-linecap=\\"round\\" stroke-linejoin=\\"round\\" stroke-width=\\"1.5\\" d=\\"M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z\\"></path>\\n            </svg>\\n          </div>\\n          <div>\\n            <p class=\\"text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-space-accent font-bold\\">SpacePoint FZC</p>\\n            <p class=\\"text-white font-semibold text-lg\\">Terms & Conditions of Service</p>\\n          </div>\\n        </div>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">1.</span> Introduction\\n          </h2>\\n          <p>Welcome to SpacePoint. By accessing our website, programs, or services—including SatKit, workshops, and training, you agree to these Terms & Conditions.</p>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">2.</span> Eligibility\\n          </h2>\\n          <ul class=\\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-space-light/75\\">\\n            <li>Our programs are designed for students, educators, and institutions.</li>\\n            <li>Participants under 18 require parental or institutional consent.</li>\\n          </ul>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">3.</span> Our Services\\n          </h2>\\n          <p class=\\"mb-3\\">SpacePoint provides:</p>\\n          <ul class=\\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-space-light/75\\">\\n            <li>Satellite development programs (online, onsite, hybrid)</li>\\n            <li>Hands-on kits (e.g., SatKit)</li>\\n            <li>Workshops, camps, and training sessions</li>\\n            <li>Instructor training and certifications</li>\\n          </ul>\\n          <p class=\\"mt-3 italic text-space-light/70\\">We may update or modify our services at any time.</p>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">4.</span> Program Delivery\\n          </h2>\\n          <p class=\\"mb-3\\">SpacePoint programs may be delivered in one of the following formats:</p>\\n          <ul class=\\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-space-light/75\\">\\n            <li><strong>Online:</strong> Virtual sessions</li>\\n            <li><strong>Onsite:</strong> In-person at schools, events, or partner locations</li>\\n            <li><strong>Hybrid:</strong> Combination of both</li>\\n          </ul>\\n          <p class=\\"mt-3\\">The delivery mode will be communicated before the program starts.</p>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">5.</span> Online Participation\\n          </h2>\\n          <p class=\\"mb-3\\">Participants are responsible for having:</p>\\n          <ul class=\\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-space-light/75\\">\\n            <li>A stable internet connection</li>\\n            <li>A suitable device (laptop or tablet)</li>\\n          </ul>\\n          <p class=\\"mt-4 mb-2 font-semibold text-white\\">SpacePoint is not responsible for:</p>\\n          <ul class=\\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-space-light/75\\">\\n            <li>Connectivity issues</li>\\n            <li>Device malfunctions</li>\\n            <li>Third-party platform disruptions</li>\\n          </ul>\\n          <p class=\\"mt-3 italic text-space-light/70\\">Sessions may be recorded for quality, training, or educational purposes.</p>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">6.</span> Onsite Participation\\n          </h2>\\n          <ul class=\\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-space-light/75\\">\\n            <li>Participants must follow all safety instructions and use equipment responsibly.</li>\\n            <li>Any misuse or negligence resulting in damage may result in charges.</li>\\n            <li><strong>For institutional programs:</strong> The hosting organization is responsible for general supervision outside session delivery.</li>\\n          </ul>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">7.</span> Registration & Accounts\\n          </h2>\\n          <ul class=\\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-space-light/75\\">\\n            <li>Users must provide accurate and complete information.</li>\\n            <li>SpacePoint may suspend access for incorrect or misleading data.</li>\\n          </ul>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">8.</span> Payments\\n          </h2>\\n          <ul class=\\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-space-light/75\\">\\n            <li>Fees must be paid in advance unless otherwise agreed.</li>\\n            <li>Pricing may vary depending on program type or partner agreements.</li>\\n          </ul>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">9.</span> Refunds & Cancellations\\n          </h2>\\n          <p class=\\"mb-3 font-semibold text-white\\">Refunds are only provided if:</p>\\n          <ul class=\\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 mb-4 text-space-light/75\\">\\n            <li>A program is canceled by SpacePoint</li>\\n          </ul>\\n          <p class=\\"mb-3 font-semibold text-white\\">Refunds are not provided for:</p>\\n          <ul class=\\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-space-light/75\\">\\n            <li>Missed sessions</li>\\n            <li>Partial attendance</li>\\n            <li>Withdrawal after program start</li>\\n          </ul>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">10.</span> Attendance & Scheduling\\n          </h2>\\n          <ul class=\\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-space-light/75\\">\\n            <li>Participants are expected to attend all sessions.</li>\\n            <li>Missed sessions are not guaranteed to be rescheduled.</li>\\n            <li>SpacePoint may reschedule sessions or assign alternative instructors if needed.</li>\\n          </ul>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">11.</span> Intellectual Property\\n          </h2>\\n          <p class=\\"mb-3\\">\\n            All materials, including SatKit, curriculum, content and documentation, are owned by SpacePoint and protected by law.\\n          </p>\\n          <p>They may only be used for personal educational purposes and may not be copied, shared, or resold without permission.</p>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">12.</span> Code of Conduct\\n          </h2>\\n          <p class=\\"mb-3\\">\\n            Participants must respect instructors and peers, follow program guidelines, and use tools and equipment responsibly.\\n          </p>\\n          <p>Violation may result in removal without refund.</p>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">13.</span> Media & Recording\\n          </h2>\\n          <p class=\\"mb-3\\">\\n            By participating in our programs, photos, videos, or recordings may be captured and used for educational or promotional purposes.\\n          </p>\\n          <p>For minors, consent is assumed through parents, guardians, or institutions unless withdrawn in writing.</p>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">14.</span> Limitation of Liability\\n          </h2>\\n          <ul class=\\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-space-light/75\\">\\n            <li>SpacePoint is not liable for indirect or incidental damages.</li>\\n            <li>Liability is limited to the amount paid for the service.</li>\\n          </ul>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section>\\n          <h2 class=\\"font-outfit font-bold text-xl text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\\">\\n            <span class=\\"text-space-accent\\">15.</span> Governing Law\\n          </h2>\\n          <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of the United Arab Emirates. Any dispute arising out of or related to these terms shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the UAE courts.</p>\\n        </section>", "display_order": 2, "is_active": true, "show_in_footer": true}, {"slug": "shipping-policy", "title": "Shipping & Delivery Policy", "eyebrow": "Operations & Logistics", "meta": "Version 1.0 · Effective 25 October 2026 · Approved by Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder & CEO", "summary": "", "content_html": "<p class=\\"lead\\"><strong>UAE shipping:</strong> AED 20 per order up to and including AED 500. <strong>Free UAE shipping:</strong> orders over AED 500. International shipping: quoted individually; customs charges are generally the customer’s responsibility.</p><section><h2>1. Overview</h2><p>This policy applies to physical goods purchased from SpacePoint, including educational kits, learning hardware, components and related products. It explains our standard shipping charges, international quotation process and delivery responsibilities.</p></section>\\n<section><h2>2. Our Logistics Partner</h2><p>SpacePoint generally arranges deliveries through Jeebly, subject to courier availability, destination, shipment specifications and service restrictions. We may use another approved courier where necessary.</p></section>\\n<section><h2>3. Shipping Within the United Arab Emirates</h2><p>For standard deliveries within supported locations in the UAE, delivery costs AED 20 per order when the total value of products in that order is AED 500 or less. Where the total product value of an order exceeds AED 500, standard UAE delivery is free of charge and paid for by SpacePoint. The threshold is calculated per order before shipping fees; orders of exactly AED 500 incur AED 20 delivery. Any exceptional delivery requirement or special handling charge will be communicated before the order is confirmed.</p></section>\\n<section><h2>4. International Delivery Quotations</h2><p>SpacePoint may arrange shipments outside the UAE depending on the destination and the availability of suitable logistics services. International delivery is quoted separately and is not included in the UAE free-delivery offer. We generally request an individual quotation from Jeebly or another approved delivery partner based on the destination, parcel dimensions, weight, product type and delivery requirements. The quotation is then shared with the customer for approval before shipment. The agreed shipping amount is included in the customer’s total order or delivery quotation; no universal international delivery fee applies.</p></section>\\n<section><h2>5. Customs, Clearance and Import Charges</h2><p>For international orders, customs clearance procedures and any customs duties, import taxes, destination VAT, inspection fees and related government or brokerage charges are the customer’s responsibility, unless SpacePoint expressly agrees otherwise in writing. These charges are separate from the international shipping quotation unless that quotation clearly states they are included. The customer is responsible for satisfying destination-country import requirements; SpacePoint will provide reasonably available commercial invoices and product information to support customs documentation.</p></section>\\n<section><h2>6. Processing and Delivery Estimates</h2><p>Orders are prepared for dispatch after confirmation and any applicable payment requirements. Processing and estimated transit times depend on stock availability, kit assembly or customization, destination and courier schedules. Time estimates communicated at checkout or in a quotation are indicative unless a specific delivery date is expressly agreed. International shipments may be delayed by customs processing or factors outside SpacePoint’s reasonable control.</p></section>\\n<section><h2>7. Delivery Details and Tracking</h2><p>Customers must provide a complete and accurate delivery address, recipient name and working contact number. Tracking information will be provided when available through our courier partner. A recipient should be available to accept delivery or follow courier instructions. We cannot guarantee delivery to every address or P.O. box; unsupported destinations will be communicated before dispatch.</p></section>\\n<section><h2>8. Failed Deliveries, Address Changes and Additional Charges</h2><p>A failed delivery due to incomplete or incorrect details, recipient unavailability or a post-dispatch address change may require a new shipment or redelivery fee. Where additional fees arise, SpacePoint will advise the customer before arranging the requested service, where practical.</p></section>\\n<section><h2>9. Damaged, Missing or Incorrect Items</h2><p>Please inspect packages promptly on delivery. If items arrive damaged, missing or incorrect, contact info@spacepoint.ae with the order reference and photographs where available. SpacePoint will review the issue and coordinate an appropriate solution with the courier or customer, taking account of applicable consumer rights. Nothing in this policy limits non-excludable rights under applicable law.</p></section>\\n<section><h2>10. Contact and Policy Updates</h2><p>For delivery questions or international shipping quotations, contact info@spacepoint.ae. Secondary contact and escalation: Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder &amp; CEO, a.alsalmani@spacepoint.ae. SpacePoint may update this policy prospectively; changes do not retrospectively alter already confirmed delivery terms without agreement.</p></section>", "display_order": 3, "is_active": true, "show_in_footer": true}, {"slug": "anti-bribery", "title": "Anti-Bribery & Anti-Corruption Policy", "eyebrow": "Corporate Governance & Sustainability", "meta": "Approved by Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder & CEO · 25 October 2026", "summary": "Anti-Bribery & Anti-Corruption Policy — official SpacePoint public information and contact details.", "content_html": "<p>Anti-Bribery &amp; Anti-Corruption Policy</p><p>Public policy · Approved for website publication</p><h2>1. Purpose and Commitment</h2><p>SpacePoint maintains zero tolerance for bribery, corruption, kickbacks and improper influence. We compete fairly and make decisions based on merit, quality, transparent criteria and lawful commercial considerations. This policy applies to directors, officers, employees, interns, contractors, instructors, agents and third parties acting for or representing SpacePoint.</p><h2>2. Prohibited Conduct</h2><p>No covered person may directly or indirectly offer, promise, authorize, request, accept or provide anything of value to improperly obtain or retain business, influence a decision, secure an unfair advantage, or reward improper conduct. This includes cash, gifts, entertainment, travel, employment opportunities, discounts, sponsorships, charitable contributions and benefits channeled through intermediaries.</p><h2>3. Public Officials and Educational Institutions</h2><p>Interactions with government agencies, public institutions, state-owned entities, schools, universities and procurement teams demand heightened care. No payment, benefit or advantage may be offered to influence official or procurement decisions. Any government-related hospitality or benefit must be lawful, transparent, modest and pre-approved where required.</p><h2>4. Gifts, Hospitality and Expenses</h2><p>Modest business courtesies may be permissible only when lawful, occasional, proportionate, openly recorded and not linked to a decision or tender. Cash and cash equivalents are forbidden. Team members must disclose gifts or hospitality that could create an appearance of influence. The company will establish and maintain internal monetary approval thresholds and a gifts register; until those are formally issued, seek written management approval before offering or accepting any material benefit.</p><h2>5. Facilitation Payments and Third Parties</h2><p>Facilitation payments are prohibited, even if described as customary, except where a person faces an immediate threat to health or safety; such circumstances must be reported promptly and documented. Business partners, resellers, agents and consultants must be vetted proportionately and may not be used to do indirectly what SpacePoint is prohibited from doing directly.</p><h2>6. Procurement, Conflicts and Sponsorship</h2><p>Supplier selection, sponsorship, recruitment, grants, awards and contract decisions must be fair and documented. Personal, family or financial conflicts of interest must be disclosed and managed. Sponsorships and charitable support must have legitimate purposes, be approved and properly recorded; they must not disguise improper payments.</p><h2>7. Accurate Books and Records</h2><p>All payments, discounts, reimbursements, gifts, donations and expenses must have genuine descriptions, appropriate supporting records and authorized approvals. False invoices, undisclosed funds, off-book accounts and misleading entries are prohibited.</p><h2>8. Reporting and Non-Retaliation</h2><p>Anyone who suspects bribery or corruption should use SpacePoint’s whistleblowing channel: hr@spacepoint.ae. SpacePoint prohibits retaliation against anyone raising a concern in good faith or cooperating in an investigation.</p><h2>9. Review, Investigation and Consequences</h2><p>Reports will be assessed impartially, with confidentiality maintained as far as practicable. Proven violations may result in corrective action, termination of engagement, recovery of losses or referral to competent authorities, consistent with applicable law. This policy is reviewed at least annually and following significant incidents.</p><h2>Policy accountability and approval</h2><p>Policy owner: SpacePoint management (designated policy owner to be assigned internally). Approved by: Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder &amp; CEO. Review cycle: At least annually or sooner if legal or operational requirements change.</p><h2>Publication, Contacts and Approval</h2><p>Approved by: Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder &amp; CEO, SpacePoint.</p><p>Publication date: 25 October 2026. Review: At least annually and when relevant legal or operational changes occur.</p><p>Primary contact: info@spacepoint.ae. Secondary contact / escalation: a.alsalmani@spacepoint.ae.</p>", "display_order": 4, "is_active": true, "show_in_footer": true}, {"slug": "code-of-conduct", "title": "Business & Supplier Code of Conduct", "eyebrow": "Corporate Governance & Sustainability", "meta": "Approved by Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder & CEO · 25 October 2026", "summary": "Business & Supplier Code of Conduct — official SpacePoint public information and contact details.", "content_html": "<p>Business &amp; Supplier Code of Conduct</p><p>Public policy · Based on SpacePoint Employee Handbook and Code of Conduct (May 2026)</p><h2>Relationship to the employee handbook</h2><p>This external-facing Code summarizes standards in SpacePoint Employee Handbook and Code of Conduct, Version 1.0 (May 2026), particularly professional conduct, conflicts of interest, youth safeguarding, confidentiality, safety and reporting. The employee handbook remains the more detailed internal reference. Additional supplier requirements below are proposed for management approval.</p><p>Business Code of Ethics &amp; Supplier Code of Conduct</p><h2>1. Values and Applicability</h2><p>SpacePoint expects integrity, respect, professionalism, accountability and responsible innovation in every interaction. This Code applies to employees, leadership, interns, instructors, contractors and representatives. Suppliers and other business partners are expected to follow the supplier standards described here when working with SpacePoint.</p><h2>2. Compliance and Honest Dealings</h2><p>We comply with applicable laws and contractual commitments, communicate truthfully, avoid deceptive marketing, keep accurate records and conduct fair competition. No one may conceal material facts, misrepresent qualifications, misuse confidential information or gain an unfair advantage through improper means.</p><h2>3. Equal Opportunity, Respect and Safeguarding</h2><p>We prohibit harassment, bullying, discrimination, intimidation and abusive conduct. We promote an inclusive, professional learning environment and safeguard children and other vulnerable participants. Personnel interacting with minors must follow applicable safeguarding procedures, appropriate supervision and approved photography/communication rules.</p><h2>4. Conflicts of Interest</h2><p>Employees and representatives must promptly disclose relationships or interests that could compromise objective decisions, including supplier ownership, family connections, outside work, gifts and procurement involvement. Disclosed conflicts will be assessed and managed, including recusal where appropriate.</p><h2>5. Confidentiality, Privacy and Intellectual Property</h2><p>Protect participant and customer information, institutional data, prototypes, designs, curriculum, software, source code and proprietary materials. Use information only for authorized purposes. Respect the intellectual-property rights of SpacePoint, students, collaborators and third parties, subject to the agreed ownership and licensing terms.</p><h2>6. Product Quality, Safety and Responsible Learning</h2><p>We strive to provide accurate technical guidance, appropriately tested educational kits, clear safety instructions and responsible handling of electrical, mechanical, chemical and flight-related activities. Instructors and suppliers must report unsafe conditions, defective items, incidents and material quality concerns without delay.</p><h2>7. Anti-Corruption and Fair Procurement</h2><p>Bribery, kickbacks, bid manipulation and undisclosed conflicts are prohibited. Procurement decisions should consider objective criteria, including price, quality, safety, capability, lead time and compliance. Gifts or personal benefits must not influence supplier evaluation.</p><h2>8. Environmental and Social Responsibility</h2><p>We encourage responsible sourcing, reduction of unnecessary waste, safe handling and disposal of batteries and electronics, and efficient use of materials. We do not tolerate forced labor, trafficking, or unlawful child labor and expect suppliers to follow applicable labor and occupational safety requirements.</p><h2>9. Supplier-Specific Expectations</h2><p>Suppliers must maintain lawful licenses and permits where required; ensure safe working conditions; honor confidentiality and data-protection obligations; avoid bribery and conflicts; provide authentic and conforming goods and services; accurately state country of origin and product specifications; maintain traceable business records; disclose relevant subcontracting where material; and notify SpacePoint promptly of significant compliance incidents affecting our engagement.</p><h2>10. Raising Concerns and Enforcement</h2><p>Employees, learners, customers and suppliers may report suspected misconduct using hr@spacepoint.ae. Good-faith reporting is protected by SpacePoint’s non-retaliation commitment. SpacePoint may investigate concerns and take proportionate corrective action, up to suspension or termination of a business relationship, subject to contracts and law.</p><h2>11. Acknowledgement and Governance</h2><p>Personnel and relevant suppliers may be required to acknowledge this Code as part of onboarding or contracting. SpacePoint management is responsible for implementation, periodic communication, and at least annual review of this Code.</p><h2>Policy accountability and approval</h2><p>Policy owner: SpacePoint management (designated policy owner to be assigned internally). Approved by: Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder &amp; CEO. Review cycle: At least annually or sooner if legal or operational requirements change.</p><p>If an inconsistency is identified between this public summary and the internal handbook, SpacePoint management will review and resolve it. Supplier clauses take effect through relevant contracts, purchase orders or supplier acknowledgements.</p><h2>Publication, Contacts and Approval</h2><p>Approved by: Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder &amp; CEO, SpacePoint.</p><p>Publication date: 25 October 2026. Review: At least annually and when relevant legal or operational changes occur.</p><p>Primary contact: hr@spacepoint.ae. Secondary contact / escalation: a.alsalmani@spacepoint.ae.</p>", "display_order": 5, "is_active": true, "show_in_footer": true}, {"slug": "speak-up", "title": "Whistleblowing & Non-Retaliation Policy", "eyebrow": "Corporate Governance & Sustainability", "meta": "Approved by Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder & CEO · 25 October 2026", "summary": "Whistleblowing & Non-Retaliation Policy — official SpacePoint public information and contact details.", "content_html": "<p>Whistleblowing &amp; Non-Retaliation Policy</p><p>Public policy · Reporting channel activation pending</p><h2>1. Purpose and Who Can Report</h2><p>SpacePoint encourages employees, contractors, interns, instructors, learners, parents, suppliers, customers and other stakeholders to report reasonable concerns about misconduct safely and promptly. Reports may concern behavior involving SpacePoint, its activities, personnel, or business partners.</p><h2>2. Matters That May Be Reported</h2><p>Examples include bribery, fraud, theft, conflicts of interest, misuse of funds, serious policy or legal breaches, falsification of records, data misuse, cybersecurity incidents, serious health and safety risks, safeguarding concerns, harassment, discrimination, retaliation, and deliberate concealment of wrongdoing. Ordinary service requests and employment grievances may be redirected to the appropriate channel without disregarding a serious underlying concern.</p><h2>3. Reporting Channels</h2><p>Primary reporting channel: hr@spacepoint.ae. Alternative escalation: Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder &amp; CEO (a.alsalmani@spacepoint.ae); where a concern involves the CEO, request referral to a non-conflicted company decision-maker. For urgent threats to personal safety, contact local emergency services or competent authorities immediately. These reporting channels must be operational and monitored before this policy is published as an active mechanism.</p><h2>4. Anonymous Reports and Information to Include</h2><p>A reporter may choose not to identify themselves, but ordinary email does not provide guaranteed anonymity. If anonymity is important, the reporter should consider appropriate alternative reporting routes available under applicable law; limited information may make follow-up difficult. Reports should include what happened, when, where, who may be involved, any supporting evidence, and a safe method for follow-up if the reporter chooses to provide one. Do not obtain evidence through unlawful access or share sensitive material more widely than necessary.</p><h2>5. Handling Procedure and Target Timelines</h2><p>The designated recipient logs and safeguards each report, screens for urgency and conflicts, and assigns a suitable impartial reviewer. Where contact details are provided, SpacePoint targets acknowledgement within five business days and an initial assessment within ten business days. Investigations are conducted as promptly as practical; periodic updates may be provided where lawful and appropriate. These are internal service targets, not guaranteed legal deadlines.</p><h2>6. Confidentiality and Fairness</h2><p>Information is shared only with those who need it to assess, investigate or resolve the matter, or where disclosure is legally required. The identity of a reporter will be protected to the extent reasonably possible, but absolute secrecy or anonymity cannot be guaranteed. Individuals named in allegations will be treated fairly and given an appropriate opportunity to respond where consistent with a sound investigation.</p><h2>7. Non-Retaliation</h2><p>SpacePoint prohibits dismissal, threats, harassment, intimidation, adverse assignments, denial of opportunities, supplier exclusion or other detrimental treatment because someone raises a concern in good faith or assists an inquiry. Suspected retaliation should be reported immediately and investigated separately. This commitment is a company policy and does not imply a particular statutory protected-disclosure status for every report.</p><h2>8. Outcomes, Records and Escalation</h2><p>The reviewer documents findings and recommended corrective actions, which may include process changes, training, disciplinary measures or appropriate referral to competent authorities. Cases and evidence are held securely with restricted access and retained according to legal requirements and a defined internal retention schedule. Management will review aggregate trends without exposing reporters unnecessarily.</p><h2>9. Good-Faith Reports and Misuse</h2><p>A report need not be proven correct to receive good-faith protection; reasonable concerns are sufficient. Knowingly false allegations or deliberately fabricated evidence may be treated as misconduct, following a fair review. Individuals are not discouraged from making reports to competent authorities where permitted or required by law.</p><h2>10. Governance and Review</h2><p>The designated governance owner administers this mechanism and reports material matters to non-conflicted company leadership. If a complaint concerns the designated recipient, it must be routed to the alternative independent contact. This policy will be reviewed at least annually and after serious incidents.</p><h2>Policy accountability and approval</h2><p>Policy owner: SpacePoint management (designated policy owner to be assigned internally). Approved by: Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder &amp; CEO. Review cycle: At least annually or sooner if legal or operational requirements change.</p><h2>Publication, Contacts and Approval</h2><p>Approved by: Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder &amp; CEO, SpacePoint.</p><p>Publication date: 25 October 2026. Review: At least annually and when relevant legal or operational changes occur.</p><p>Primary contact: hr@spacepoint.ae. Secondary contact / escalation: a.alsalmani@spacepoint.ae.</p><p>For concerns involving the usual recipient, contact the CEO using the secondary email. If the CEO is implicated, request reassignment to a non-conflicted responsible decision-maker. No channel can guarantee absolute confidentiality; access will be limited on a need-to-know basis.</p>", "display_order": 6, "is_active": true, "show_in_footer": true}, {"slug": "impact", "title": "ESG Strategy 2026–2028", "eyebrow": "Corporate Governance & Sustainability", "meta": "Approved by Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder & CEO · 25 October 2026", "summary": "ESG Strategy 2026–2028 — official SpacePoint public information and contact details.", "content_html": "<p>ESG Strategy &amp; Sustainability Commitments 2026–2028</p><p>Public strategy · Approved for website publication</p><p>ESG Strategy &amp; Sustainability Commitments</p><p>This is a forward-looking strategy, not an audited ESG performance report. Proposed targets are identified as aspirations, subject to baseline measurement, resources, and periodic review; they are not presented as achieved results.</p><h2>Executive summary</h2><p>SpacePoint develops practical pathways into space science, satellite engineering and advanced technology through modular educational hardware, training, digital learning and partnerships. Our greatest opportunity for positive impact is to widen access to meaningful STEM learning, develop future-ready skills and encourage responsible innovation. Our principal environmental priorities are resource-conscious kit design, electronic-waste management and travel-efficient delivery; our governance priorities are integrity, learner safety, privacy and transparent business conduct.</p><p>Our ambition is to contribute toward one million learners over the long term. This aspiration is distinct from the measurable 2026–2028 ESG targets below and is not a claim of present reach.</p><h2>01 / Our ESG approach</h2><p>This strategy covers SpacePoint-controlled activities and relevant supplier and delivery-partner relationships in the UAE and other countries where programs are delivered. It is informed by the UN Sustainable Development Goals (especially SDGs 4, 8, 9, 10, 12, 13, 16 and 17) and by GRI principles for identifying material impacts; SpacePoint does not claim GRI-compliant reporting, certification, independent assurance or UN endorsement.</p><h2>02 / Environmental responsibility</h2><p>Objective: deliver high-quality hands-on STEM education while reducing avoidable materials, waste and operational impacts.</p><p>Design educational kits for repeated classroom use, modular repair and replacement of individual components rather than unnecessary full-kit disposal.</p><p>Develop reusable packaging and maintain a take-back, repair or component recovery pathway where operationally feasible.</p><p>Handle batteries, printed circuit boards and electronic waste through suitable authorized collection and recycling arrangements.</p><p>Expand digital simulation, hybrid instruction and remote mentoring when educationally effective, while retaining hands-on practical learning.</p><p>Integrate energy efficiency, environmental sensing, Earth observation and climate-related projects into relevant teaching pathways.</p><p>Establish a defensible baseline for kit materials, waste, program travel and electricity before making emissions-reduction claims.</p><h2>03 / Social impact and inclusion</h2><p>Objective: make space and advanced-technology learning more accessible, engaging, safe and connected to tangible careers.</p><p>Offer age-appropriate pathways from introductory STEM activities to satellite development, prototyping, technical projects and research exposure.</p><p>Maintain Arabic- and English-language learning resources where practical, together with adaptable delivery for schools, universities and community partners.</p><p>Use sponsored cohorts, school and institutional partnerships, scholarships or subsidized access when funded and feasible to reach learners who face financial or geographic barriers.</p><p>Develop instructor capacity through train-the-trainer programs, assessment and ongoing improvement of educational quality.</p><p>Maintain child safeguarding, photo-consent, data-protection, accessibility and safety arrangements for programs involving minors.</p><p>Track participation, course completion, learning outcomes and student progression; seek disaggregated participation data only where lawful, appropriate and voluntarily provided.</p><h2>04 / Governance, ethics and accountability</h2><p>Objective: operate with integrity, lawful conduct, documented controls and respectful channels to raise concerns.</p><p>Adopt and maintain the Data Protection, Privacy &amp; Information Security Policy, Anti-Bribery &amp; Anti-Corruption Policy, Business &amp; Supplier Code of Conduct, and Whistleblowing &amp; Non-Retaliation Policy.</p><p>Assign executive oversight and a designated owner for ESG measurement, review and stakeholder inquiries.</p><p>Use fair supplier-selection criteria, conflict-of-interest disclosure, accurate records and proportionate due diligence.</p><p>Provide confidential channels for misconduct, safeguarding and privacy concerns, with protection from retaliation for good-faith reports.</p><p>Review material ESG risks at least annually and investigate significant incidents, including product safety and information security concerns.</p><p>Publish a concise annual progress update that identifies measured results, target changes, data limitations and material incidents where disclosure is lawful and appropriate.</p><h2>05 / Proposed 2026–2028 scorecard</h2><p>The targets below are proposed future objectives, not achieved results or guaranteed outcomes. Year one establishes consistent counting rules and baselines; subsequent targets should be refined after the baseline review.</p><h2>06 / Material topics and stakeholder engagement</h2><p>Initial material topics include learner access and skills, child safety, data privacy and cybersecurity, instructional quality and product safety, fair employment and instructor welfare, anti-corruption, supply-chain integrity, materials and electronic waste, and responsible use of technology. This list is a management working assessment—not the result of a completed formal materiality study.</p><p>We will gather feedback from learners, guardians, educators, institutional partners, instructors, employees and suppliers using appropriate surveys, program debriefs and dedicated reporting channels. We will document how that feedback informs priorities.</p><h2>07 / Implementation roadmap</h2><h2>08 / Governance and reporting</h2><p>Executive sponsor: SpacePoint CEO or designated executive. Operational owners: education/programs, product development, operations and information security, as assigned in an approved responsibility matrix. The executive sponsor reviews the scorecard at least annually and approves public disclosures. Material concerns must also use the relevant formal reporting, privacy, safety or whistleblowing process without waiting for annual review.</p><p>Metric definitions should prevent double counting, separate enrolled learners from completed learners, distinguish planned from delivered activities, and retain supporting evidence. Data about students and minors should be reported in aggregate and handled according to the privacy policy.</p><h2>09 / Public commitments</h2><p>We commit to measuring what matters, improving how we deliver programs and products, providing respectful and inclusive learning environments, safeguarding students and their information, engaging suppliers fairly, and communicating progress without overstating outcomes. We will update this strategy as our capabilities and stakeholder needs evolve.</p><h2>References and alignment</h2><p>GRI 3: Material Topics (2021), globalreporting.org/publications/documents/english/gri-3-material-topics-2021/; United Nations Sustainable Development Goals, sdgs.un.org/goals. These are alignment references, not evidence of certification or conformance.</p><h2>Publication, Contacts and Approval</h2><p>Approved by: Abdullah AlSalmani, Co-Founder &amp; CEO, SpacePoint.</p><p>Publication date: 25 October 2026. Review: At least annually and when relevant legal or operational changes occur.</p><p>Primary contact: info@spacepoint.ae. Secondary contact / escalation: a.alsalmani@spacepoint.ae.</p><p>This strategy outlines direction and proposed objectives. It is not an assurance statement, audit or certification, and does not itself establish performance against all targets.</p><div class=\\"table-wrap\\"><table><tr><th>Topic / indicator</th><th>2026 baseline or action</th><th>Proposed target by end-2028</th></tr><tr><td>Educational reach</td><td>Validate unique learner count across LMS and offline registers</td><td>Report annual unique learners and year-on-year growth; set a numeric expansion target after baseline</td></tr><tr><td>Instructor development</td><td>Validate certified instructor register</td><td>Publish annual number of instructors trained/certified and active</td></tr><tr><td>Learning outcomes</td><td>Adopt pre/post assessment and completion definitions</td><td>Measure outcomes for at least 80% of eligible structured cohorts</td></tr><tr><td>Inclusive access</td><td>Identify subsidized/sponsored places and relevant consented demographics</td><td>Report number and share of subsidized places annually</td></tr><tr><td>Kit circularity</td><td>Inventory reusable kit parts, repairs and disposals</td><td>Apply documented repair/reuse practices to all new kit product lines</td></tr><tr><td>Electronic waste</td><td>Establish collection log and approved disposal route</td><td>Log 100% of electronic waste handed over through formal company processes</td></tr><tr><td>Data &amp; safeguarding</td><td>Assign policy owners, train affected staff and document incidents</td><td>Annual policy and safeguarding review; report completion and improvements</td></tr><tr><td>Ethics &amp; supplier conduct</td><td>Approve policy suite, supplier onboarding and reporting channels</td><td>Code acknowledgement for all material new suppliers and relevant team members</td></tr><tr><td>ESG disclosure</td><td>Publish this strategy after approval and start KPI register</td><td>Publish a progress update each year</td></tr></table></div><div class=\\"table-wrap\\"><table><tr><th>Period</th><th>Priority actions</th><th>Evidence / owner</th></tr><tr><td>Q4 2026</td><td>Approve strategy and governance policies; appoint owners; validate student metrics and reporting method</td><td>Management approval; KPI dictionary; policy register</td></tr><tr><td>2027 H1</td><td>Launch ESG register; apply consent, safeguarding and supplier procedures; establish waste and repair logs</td><td>Program operations; product lead; ESG owner</td></tr><tr><td>2027 H2</td><td>Review data quality and material topics; refine numerical targets; assess partner feedback</td><td>ESG review minutes; revised scorecard</td></tr><tr><td>2028</td><td>Improve circularity and inclusive delivery; publish year-on-year impact and governance update</td><td>Annual public ESG update with limitations</td></tr></table></div>", "display_order": 7, "is_active": true, "show_in_footer": true}]')

async def seed_default_policies(db: AsyncSession):
    existing_count = (await db.execute(select(func.count(WebsitePolicy.id)))).scalar() or 0
    if existing_count > 0:
        return
    for item in DEFAULT_POLICIES:
        row = WebsitePolicy(
            slug=item['slug'],
            title=item['title'],
            eyebrow=item.get('eyebrow'),
            meta=item.get('meta'),
            summary=item.get('summary'),
            content_html=item['content_html'],
            display_order=item.get('display_order', 0),
            is_active=item.get('is_active', True),
            show_in_footer=item.get('show_in_footer', True),
        )
        db.add(row)
    await db.commit()
